## Sambhav's Contribution

I worked on debugging and improving both parts after testing the code.

In `cipher.py`, I fixed the uppercase range so the first condition correctly
uses A-M. I also worked on the decryption part so the shifts can be reversed
properly. I checked the number shifting with modulo 10 and worked with
`encrypt_file()`, `decrypt_file()` and `verify_files()` to make sure the file
encryption and decryption process works correctly.

In `evaluator.py`, I worked on some problems I found while testing the parser.
I fixed unary negative handling and the power operation so expressions like
`2 ^ 3 ^ 2` and `2 ^ -2` are parsed correctly. I also worked on implicit
multiplication for expressions like `2(3 + 4)` and `(2)3`, and checked error
cases such as invalid characters and division by zero.

After making these changes, I tested the programs with different inputs to
check that the changes were working as expected.
